{{Quote|I had a vision of the Throne of the Sith, and who was on it.''"<br />"''Ren?''"<br />"''And me.|[[Rey Skywalker]] and [[Finn]]|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
The '''Throne of the Sith''', also called the '''Dark Throne''', was the [[Sith]] [[throne]] of [[Exegol]], located within the [[Sith Citadel]]'s [[Sith cultist|Sith loyalist]] [[Amphitheater of the Sith Eternal|chamber]].<ref name="TROS VD" /> [[Darth Sidious]], the [[Galactic Emperor]] and reigning [[Dark Lord of the Sith]], prepared the throne as his permanent seat of power for an eternal [[Sith Empire]].<ref name="The Star Wars Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> The throne was destroyed by Rey along with [[Darth]] Sidious during the [[Battle of Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

{{Stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Throne of the Sith first appeared in the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], the third installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[sequel trilogy]].<ref name="Episode IX" /> The Dark Throne bears similarity to the [[Emperor's Throne Room]] thumbnail sketches shown in ''[[Star Wars Art: Ralph McQuarrie]]''. Made in [[1981]] by ''Star Wars'' concept artist [[Ralph McQuarrie]], they were intended for use in the [[1983]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Ralph McQuarrie">''[[Star Wars Art: Ralph McQuarrie]]''</ref>

